# Google Drive integration
#
# Both values below are inlined into the shipped JS bundle by Vite
# (that's what the `VITE_` prefix opts into). They are NOT secrets —
# do not put server-side credentials behind the `VITE_` prefix.
#
# Create credentials at https://console.cloud.google.com/ following
# docs/plans/google-drive-integration.md §4 (restrict the API key to
# HTTP referrers `annot.work` + `localhost:3000` so a scraped copy is
# useless off-origin).
#
# For local dev, copy this file to `.env.local` in this directory.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=your-api-key

# GitHub integration (individual-user storage backend)
#
# Register an OAuth App at https://github.com/settings/developers
# ("New OAuth App"). The client ID is inlined into the bundle — it's
# public by design; GitHub's OAuth App model treats the client ID as
# non-secret when Device Flow is enabled. No client secret is used.
#
# Requirements on the OAuth App settings page:
#   - Enable "Device Flow" (checkbox).
#   - Homepage URL: https://annot.work (or your deployment).
#   - Authorization callback URL can be anything (unused by device flow).
#
# See `docs/plans/github-integration.md` §1 for the auth design.
VITE_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=your-github-oauth-app-client-id
